# Agentic attack detections by ThreatDefence: HackSynth
# https://github.com/ThreatDefence/agentic-attack-detections
# Suricata 7 and 8. SID range 3812401-3812449.
# HackSynth has no web console and sends no fixed marker to a target, so the only network rule is for the attackbox
# setup on the host that runs it (aielte-research/HackSynth at 48a41f79, docker_setup.py:36).

# --- Attackbox setup: apt in kalilinux/kali-rolling fetches the metapackage over plain HTTP from http.kali.org ---
alert http $HOME_NET any -> $EXTERNAL_NET any (msg:"TD HackSynth attackbox setup, kali-linux-headless package download"; flow:established,to_server; http.method; content:"GET"; http.uri; content:"kali-linux-headless"; fast_pattern; classtype:policy-violation; sid:3812401; rev:1; metadata:created_at 2026_11_26, confidence Low, malware_family HackSynth, mitre_tactic_id TA0042, mitre_tactic_name Resource_Development, mitre_technique_id T1588.002, mitre_technique_name Tool;)
